1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:05,500
Good morning, Lakeside Summer Sports Camp.
Emma speaking. How can I help?

2
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:08,208
Oh, hello. I'd like to
book my son on to one of

3
00:00:08,232 --> 00:00:10,632
your summer weeks,
if there are still places.

4
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:15,820
There are, yes. Don't worry.
I'll just open a registration form.

5
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:19,100
Right, can I start with your son's name?

6
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:21,160
It's Oliver. Oliver Brandon.

7
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:23,700
And could you spell the surname for me?

8
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:29,980
Sure. B-R-A-N-D-O-N.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:33,400
Lovely. Thank you. And how old is Oliver?

10
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:36,539
Well, he's nine at the
moment, but his birthday's next

11
00:00:36,563 --> 00:00:39,092
week, so he'll be ten by
the time the camp starts.

12
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:42,747
Then I'll put ten, because we
go by age at the start of camp.

13
00:00:42,771 --> 00:00:44,452
And a contact number for you?

14
00:00:44,689 --> 00:00:50,280
My mobile's best. It's 07845-331-290.

15
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:55,080
07845-331-290.

16
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:56,336
That's it.

17
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:57,360
And your address?

18
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:03,260
27 Kestrel Close. That's K-E-S-T-R-E-L.

19
00:01:03,375 --> 00:01:06,720
Kestrel Close. And is that here in Hadley?

20
00:01:07,029 --> 00:01:10,060
No, we're just outside Hadley, actually.
We're in Ashford.

21
00:01:10,279 --> 00:01:13,540
Ashford. Lovely.
Now, which week would you like?

22
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:18,000
We run four weeks in total, but
I'm afraid week two is already full.

23
00:01:19,179 --> 00:01:22,520
We're away for week one.
So, week three, please.

24
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:26,370
Week three. And which sport
should he do as his main activity?

25
00:01:26,394 --> 00:01:28,872
He can choose football,
swimming or tennis.

26
00:01:29,369 --> 00:01:32,127
He'd probably say football,
but he did football all last

27
00:01:32,151 --> 00:01:34,772
summer, and he's really
keen to try tennis this time.

28
00:01:35,110 --> 00:01:36,120
So, let's go for tennis.

29
00:01:36,379 --> 00:01:40,140
Tennis it is. Does Oliver have any
allergies we should know about?

30
00:01:40,429 --> 00:01:43,960
He's fine with dairy and gluten
and so on, but he's allergic to nuts.

31
00:01:44,639 --> 00:01:47,093
Nuts. I'll flag that
for the kitchen staff.

32
00:01:47,117 --> 00:01:50,812
And who'll be collecting him in
the afternoons? Will that be you?

33
00:01:51,044 --> 00:01:54,600
I'm at work until six, so it'll
be his grandmother most days.

34
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:59,262
That's fine. We'll add her to the
pickup list. Last question for the form.

35
00:01:59,286 --> 00:02:01,992
How did you hear about
us? Was it our website?

36
00:02:02,599 --> 00:02:06,580
Er, no. Actually, we picked
up a leaflet at the library.

37
00:02:06,939 --> 00:02:08,680
Great. That's the form done.

38
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:12,791
Now, a few things to note
down. Normal drop-off is at nine,

39
00:02:12,815 --> 00:02:16,212
but there's an early drop-off
from 8.15, if that helps.

40
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:18,600
8.15? That's perfect for me.

41
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,003
The cost for the week is £140.

42
00:02:21,027 --> 00:02:25,332
It's gone up from last year,
I'm afraid, when it was £120.

43
00:02:26,774 --> 00:02:29,460
Everything's gone up. £140. Fine.

44
00:02:29,755 --> 00:02:33,680
Lunch isn't provided, so the children
need to bring a packed lunch every day.

45
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:37,365
And please send him with a
water bottle with his name on it.

46
00:02:37,389 --> 00:02:39,612
We get dozens that
look exactly the same.

47
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,300
I can imagine.

48
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:44,519
One more thing about
tennis. Ordinary trainers aren't

49
00:02:44,543 --> 00:02:47,632
allowed on the courts, so
he'll need proper tennis shoes.

50
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:49,980
Ah, I'll have to buy some then.

51
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:52,843
If it rains, all the outdoor
activities move into

52
00:02:52,867 --> 00:02:55,252
the sports hall, so the
day still goes ahead.

53
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,172
And on the Friday afternoon,
there's a short tournament,

54
00:02:58,196 --> 00:03:00,332
and parents are very
welcome to come and watch.

55
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:02,520
Lovely. Who does the tennis coaching?

56
00:03:02,790 --> 00:03:08,640
That's Mark Tulloch. T-U-L-L-O-C-H.
He's been with us for years.

57
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,900
Great. And when do I need to pay by?

58
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,861
Payment's due by
the 20th of June.

59
00:03:13,885 --> 00:03:17,832
Sorry, no, the 30th. The
20th was last year's date.

60
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:19,840
The 30th. Can I pay by check?

61
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:24,340
We don't take checks anymore, I'm afraid.
It's online only, through our website.

62
00:03:24,674 --> 00:03:27,280
Online? No problem.
Thanks very much for your help.

63
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:29,840
You're welcome.
We'll see Oliver in week three.

